#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
kube32-cli: build, check, deploy and ship WebAssembly pods for Kube32.

    kube32-cli build   <dir>         compile a C, Rust or AssemblyScript app to .wasm and check it
    kube32-cli check   <file.wasm>   validate a module against the app ABI
    kube32-cli deploy  <file.wasm>   create a Pod that carries the module inline (no reflash)
    kube32-cli embed   <file.wasm>   copy the module into images/ for the next firmware build
    kube32-cli sd-push <file.wasm>   copy the module onto a microSD card as kube32/images/<name>.wasm
                                     (a mounted card with --to, or a node's card over the network with --node)
    kube32-cli push    <file|dir>    upload a file or directory tree to a node's storage (kube32/<path>) through the API server
    kube32-cli firmware push <firmware.bin>   stage a firmware image on the control plane
    kube32-cli firmware rollout              update every node to the staged image, one at a time
    kube32-cli firmware status|abort|info    the rollout and each node's firmware; stop a rollout; read an image file

The ABI it checks against is include/runtime/k32_app_abi.h; the import
signatures are the m3_LinkRawFunction calls in src/runtime/app_pod.cpp and
src/runtime/host_functions.cpp, and the opcode table follows the wasm3 build
flags in CMakeLists.txt and platformio.ini. Python standard library only.

Exit codes:
    0  success
    1  input or toolchain problem (missing file or directory, compiler not found, build failed)
    2  usage error (bad arguments)
    3  the module does not satisfy the ABI (check failed)
    4  kubectl failed
    5  deploy: the pod already exists and --replace was not given; firmware rollout: one is in progress
    6  firmware rollout: the rollout failed or did not finish in time
"""
